-- title:
--   Homomorphisms killing torsion lie in the integral span
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z})^{\times}$, and let $\Gamma_H(N)$ denote the subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH N H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained as the image, under the inclusion of $\Gamma_0(N)$ into $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, of the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism $\Gamma_0(N) \to (\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z})^{\times}$ sending a matrix to the reduction of its lower right entry. Let $\kappa$ be a commutative ring, and let $x$ be an element of [`CohCarrier.H1 N H κ`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L162), that is, an additive homomorphism from the additive group $\mathrm{Additive}\,\Gamma_H(N)$ to the additive group of $\kappa$; equivalently, a group homomorphism $\Gamma_H(N) \to (\kappa, +)$. Assume that $x(\gamma) = 0$ for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_H(N)$ of finite order. Then $x$ belongs to the $\kappa$-submodule of [`CohCarrier.H1 N H κ`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L162) (with $\kappa$ acting through the target) spanned by the set of homomorphisms of the form $G$ followed by the canonical additive map $\mathbb{Z} \to \kappa$, where $G$ ranges over all homomorphisms $\Gamma_H(N) \to \mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   The statement expresses that a homomorphism from $\Gamma_H(N)$ to the additive group of a commutative ring which vanishes on all elements of finite order (the element $-1$ when present, and the elliptic elements of orders $3$, $4$, $6$) is a $\kappa$-linear combination of integer-valued homomorphisms, reflecting the fact that the torsion of the abelianisation of $\Gamma_H(N)$ is generated by the images of its finite-order elements. It rests on the description of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ modulo its centre as a free product of cyclic groups of orders $2$ and $3$, and is used in the base-change comparison [`CohCarrier.exists_linearMap_baseChange_parabolicHoms_gammaH_bot_range_eq_parabolicHoms_of_four_le`](thm.html#CohCarrier.exists_linearMap_baseChange_parabolicHoms_gammaH_bot_range_eq_parabolicHoms_of_four_le) and in the construction of Galois representations attached to eigensystems on $H^1$.
